[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-2821 agricultural/forestry machinery plant-operations coordination" "agricultural machinery plant operations actor" "ISIC 2821 implementation"], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-2821-agricultural-forestry-machinery-coverage", :adr/related ["adr-2607231500"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607992821-cloud-itonami-isic-2821-agricultural-forestry-machinery-coverage", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-15", :adr/body "# ADR-2607992821: cloud-itonami ISIC 2821 (agricultural and forestry machinery) coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted. `cloud-itonami-isic-2821` scaffolded fresh, tested green, and\npromoted `:spec` -> `:implemented` in `kotoba-lang/industry`.\n\n## Context\n\nISIC 2821 (\"Manufacture of agricultural and forestry machinery\") had\nonly a legacy placeholder entry in the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n(`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C2821`, `:maturity :spec`). Per this fleet's\nsmaller-batch rollout discipline following a prior 18-agent haiku\nbatch's 61% defect rate, this build follows the stricter verified\nprotocol (capable model, mandatory fresh-clone re-verification) that\n96+ consecutive prior agents in this fleet have completed successfully.\n\nBefore any work began, the registry's live `:name` for `{:id \"2821\"\n...}` was verified via the GitHub git blob API (not the CDN-cached\n`raw.githubusercontent.com`) against a fresh clone: it reads exactly\n\"Manufacture of agricultural and forestry machinery\", confirming the\nassigned premise. `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2821`\nreturned 404 before scaffolding started, confirming no prior attempt\nexists to build on or revert to.\n\nThe closest domain analog and mirrored reference is\n`cloud-itonami-isic-2826` (Manufacture of machinery for textile,\napparel and leather production, 77 tests / 210 assertions): both are\nback-office plant-operations-coordination actors for a fixed\nmanufacturing plant with electromechanically-assembled, test-bench-\nverified finished-goods output and a real physical/worker safety\ndimension.\n\n## Decision\n\nScaffolded `cloud-itonami-isic-2821` as a fresh standalone repo\n(`AgMachAdvisor ⊣ Agricultural and Forestry Machinery Plant Operations\nGovernor`, langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger),\nmirroring `cloud-itonami-isic-2826`'s verified module shape\nmodule-for-module (`agmachmfg.*` in place of `texmachmfg.*`):\n\n- **Equipment/product vocabulary adapted to the vertical**:\n  `:tractor-assembly-line`/`:harvester-test-bench` equipment kinds in\n  place of loom-assembly/sewing-machine-test-bench;\n  `:tractor`/`:combine-harvester`/`:tillage-implement`/`:baler`/\n  `:forestry-harvester` product-type closed set in place of weaving-\n  loom/sewing-machine/leather-cutting-machine/knitting-machine/fabric-\n  cutting-machine; `:pto-no-load-speed-rpm` (plausibility-checked\n  0-1200 rpm, informed by the ISO 500 series' nominal PTO speeds of\n  540/1000 rpm with test-bench headroom, and the ISO 4254 series'\n  general mechanical/hydraulic-safety framework) in place of\n  `:no-load-run-speed-rpm`.\n- **Four ops, all `:effect :propose` only**: `:log-production-batch`\n  (batch product-type/PTO-no-load-speed/quantity/defect-rate data\n  logging), `:schedule-maintenance` (assembly/test-bench-equipment\n  maintenance scheduling proposal), `:flag-safety-concern` (mechanical-\n  safety/hydraulic-hazard/PTO-guard-compliance concern -- ALWAYS\n  escalates regardless of confidence), `:coordinate-shipment`\n  (outbound product shipment coordination proposal).\n- **HARD invariants (twelve concrete governor checks, no override)**:\n  plant/batch record (equipment for maintenance, batch for shipment)\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action;\n  request `:effect` must be `:propose` only; the proposal's own\n  `:effect` must be within the closed propose-shaped allowlist (no\n  direct assembly/test-bench-equipment control); directly actuating\n  assembly/test-bench equipment (`:actuate-equipment? true`) is a\n  PERMANENT, unconditional block; self-issuing a machinery safety\n  certification mark (`:issue-certification? true`, any op -- e.g. CE\n  marking under the EU Machinery Directive, or ROPS certification\n  under the OECD Standard Codes for the Official Testing of\n  Agricultural and Forestry Tractors) is a PERMANENT, unconditional\n  block; a shipment may not push a batch's own recorded shipped\n  quantity past its own logged production quantity (independently\n  recomputed, never self-reported); no double-scheduling the same\n  maintenance record; no fabricated `:product-type`; no physically\n  implausible `:pto-no-load-speed-rpm` or `:defect-rate-percent`; the\n  op allowlist is closed to the four ops above.\n- **Phase 0->3 rollout**: `:schedule-maintenance`/`:flag-safety-\n  concern`/`:coordinate-shipment` are NEVER in any phase's `:auto` set\n  (permanent, matching the governor's own posture); only\n  `:log-production-batch` (no physical/financial risk) may auto-commit\n  at phase 3 when governor-clean.\n- **No pre-existing capability library to wrap** (verified: no\n  `kotoba-lang/agmachmfg`-style repo exists) -- self-contained pure-\n  function domain logic in `agmachmfg.registry`, independently\n  re-verified by `agmachmfg.governor`, the same \"ground truth, not\n  self-report\" discipline established across prior actors.\n- The blueprint's own `:itonami.blueprint/governor` keyword,\n  `:agricultural-forestry-machinery-plant-operations-governor`, is\n  grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide before this repo was created.\n\nFull module set (`registry.cljc`/`governor.cljc`/`advisor.cljc`/\n`phase.cljc`/`store.cljc`/`operation.cljc`/`sim.cljc` + `deps.edn` +\n`blueprint.edn` + governance/license docs) shipped in one fresh\nscaffold. All source is `.cljc` (portable ClojureScript/JVM/nbb) with\nno JVM-only interop, per this workspace's cljs-first runtime\npriority. The actor graph is invoked exclusively via\n`langgraph.graph/run*` (not `.invoke`, not cljs-portable).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test` from the initial scaffold: `Ran 77 tests\n  containing 210 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.`\n- `clojure -M:lint` (clj-kondo): `linting took 995ms, errors: 0,\n  warnings: 0`.\n- `clojure -M:dev:run` demo narrative exercises proposal submission,\n  escalation and every HARD-hold scenario directly (not-propose-\n  effect, unknown-op, equipment-not-verified, batch-not-verified,\n  shipment-quantity-exceeded, equipment-actuate-blocked,\n  certification-authority-blocked, already-scheduled, invalid-product-\n  type, invalid-pto-no-load-speed, invalid-defect-rate) -- confirmed\n  by inspecting the printed audit ledger (4 commits, 12 holds, no\n  exceptions).\n- Pushed to `https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2821`\n  main at commit `722faa056bbf5a3237d20e2f9bb893872c34e461`.\n- **Independently re-verified from a brand-new fresh clone** (separate\n  temp directory, `kotoba-lang/langgraph` + `kotoba-lang/langchain`\n  re-cloned as siblings): `clojure -M:test` again reports `Ran 77\n  tests containing 210 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` at the same\n  commit.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry` registry: `\"2821\"` entry's `:maturity` flipped\n  `:spec` -> `:implemented`, `:repo`/`:business-id` updated from the\n  legacy `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C2821` placeholder to\n  `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2821` via an exact-text in-place\n  edit of only that entry's block (GitHub Contents API, blob-SHA\n  match, no other entry touched). `industry_test.clj`'s\n  `:implemented` count assertion recomputed from the live file via\n  `kotoba.industry/maturity-summary` and bumped; full registry suite\n  re-run green before pushing. See PR/merge details recorded in this\n  ADR's companion EDN and the registry repo's own commit history.\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) ISIC 2821 now has a real, tested, governed plant-operations-\ncoordination actor instead of a legacy placeholder spec entry.\n\n(+) Vertical-specific hazard vocabulary (PTO entanglement, hydraulic\nhazard, ROPS certification) is explicit in the governor's domain\nmodel rather than reused verbatim from a dissimilar vertical.\n\n(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer -- no integration with real\nplant-management databases, freight dispatch or certification-body\nAPIs. Equipment actuation and certification issuance remain human-/\ninstitution-controlled via external channels.", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-15", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607992821: cloud-itonami ISIC 2821 (agricultural and forestry machinery) coverage", :adr/source-format "edn"}]